# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Local data / caches
*.log
/cache/
/data/
/build

# A local rehearsal's output, and a live miner's. `solvers.rehearse` and
# `run_miner.py` write answers and run logs here, and neither is repository
# content. Anything already committed under these paths stays tracked -- git
# ignores untracked files, never tracked ones -- so a regression fixture formed
# from archived submissions is unaffected.
#
# BOTH paths, and the second is the one that matters. `SOLVER_SOLUTION_DIR`
# defaults to the relative "solutions", resolved against the WORKING DIRECTORY,
# and both entry points are run from examples/custom_miner -- so a live miner
# archives beside itself, not at the repository root. Only the root path was
# ignored, which is the one nothing writes to: every real solve left two
# untracked files in the other, and an operator following the prompt to commit
# them would have put their own submissions into the repository.
/solutions/
/logs/
/examples/custom_miner/solutions/
/examples/custom_miner/logs/
